NOTE ON THE SOURCE DOCUMENTS IN data/raw/

The MIT licence above covers the code in this repository. It does not and
cannot cover the four source documents committed under data/raw/, which are
published by others and carry their own terms:

  EU AI Act — Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, consolidated text
    © European Union, https://eur-lex.europa.eu
    Reuse permitted with attribution (Commission Decision 2011/833/EU).

  NIST AI 100-1 (AI Risk Management Framework)
  NIST AI 600-1 (Generative AI Profile)
    Works of the US Government, in the public domain.

  OWASP LLM Top 10 (2026)
    © OWASP Foundation, CC BY-SA 4.0.

They are committed rather than downloaded on demand because regulations get
re-consolidated and repositories get reorganised, and results measured against
a document that has since changed cannot be checked. The exact bytes are the
evidence. See scripts/verify_upstream.py, which compares them against what the
publishers serve today.
